tegration tests\n\n**CLI**: `src/cli.ts` — Reads JSON from stdin, writes results to stdout, errors to stderr with exit code 1."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":776,"output":232,"cacheRead":126464,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":127472,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784950427207,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-26f113e4-12cb-4cda-81b7-2b69c63bd5e5","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 43 tests pass; `experiment-done.txt` contains \"DONE\". The exercise is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the full MHPCO Claim Office kata using strict TDD with the Red-Green-Refactor cycle:\n\n**Implementation**: `src/claim-office.ts` — Core logic for quote (premium calculation) and claim (payout calculation) operations, exposed via `processScenario()`.\n\n**Tests**: `src/claim-office.spec.ts` — 43 tests covering all spec requirements:\n- 23 premium tests (item base prices, component blocks, cursed/enchantment/loyalty/first-insurance/follow-up modifiers, rounding, integration examples)\n- 13 claim tests (standard reimbursement, deductible, high-enchantment 50% rule, dragon material, cap exhaustion, payround rounding)\n- 5 validation tests (unknown item types, items not in policy, negative damages, exceeded damage counts)\n- 2 CLI integration tests\n\n**CLI**: `src/cli.ts` — Reads JSON from stdin, writes results to stdout, errors to stderr with exit code 1."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":776,"output":232,"cacheRead":126464,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":127472,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784950427207,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-26f113e4-12cb-4cda-81b7-2b69c63bd5e5","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"}}
