nt 0 used in init = 1\n\nTotal: 12 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 24\n\nWait — previously the `0.5` was counted as a constant literal. Now it's still counted as a constant (`CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5` → the `0.5` is still a constant). So same count: 24.\n\n**Bindings** (mass 1 each):\n- 5 module-level: ITEM_PRICES, BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS, BLOCK_PRICE, EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT, PROCESSING_FEE\n- +1: CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE\n- calculateBasePremium = 1\n- items param = 1\n- counts = 1\n- total = 1\n- item (loop) = 1\n- itemBase = 1\n- type, count (destructuring) = 2\n- processScenario = 1\n- scenario param = 1\n- results = 1\n- step = 1\n- basePremium = 1\n\nTotal: 6 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 20\n\n**Invocations** (mass 2 each): Same 4 → 8\n\n**Conditionals** (mass 4 each): Same 5 → 20\n\n**Loops** (mass 5 each): 3 loops → 15\n\n**Assignments** (mass 6 each): Same 4 → 24\n\n**Total**: 24 + 20 + 8 + 20 + 15 + 24 = **111**\n\nActually, wait. Let me recheck. Before the very first measurement I had 116. After loop merge: 110. After extracting `CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE` constant: one more binding (+1 = 111). But this was an intentional trade-off: we added mass (+1) to greatly improve Rule 2 (reveals intent). As stated in the guidelines: **\"Rule 2 trumps APP: Clarity over low mass.\"**\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n\n1. **Merged duplicate item iteration** (Rule 3 - No Duplication): Combined the counting loop and the non-component pricing loop into a single pass. This eliminates redundant iteration over the same array.\n\n2. **Extracted magic number as named constant** (Rule 2 - Reveals Intent): `0.5` → `CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE`. Makes the 50% cursed surcharge immediately clear rather than a magic number buried in arithmetic.\n\n**Mass Analysis:**\n\n| Component | Before | After (merge) | After (+CURSED) |\n|-----------|--------|---------------|-----------------|\n| Constants | 24 | 24 | 24 |\n| Bindings | 20 | 19 | 20 |\n| Invocations | 8 | 8 | 8 |\n| Conditionals | 20 | 20 | 20 |\n| Loops | 20 | 15 | 15 |\n| Assignments | 24 | 24 | 24 |\n| **Total** | **116** | **110** | **111** |\n\nNet mass change: 116 → 111 (delta -5). The loop merge saved 5 mass units. The constant extraction added 1 mass unit but significantly improved readability (Rule 2 priority over APP).\n\n**Tests**: All 13 passing ✅\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Merged duplicate item iteration loop & extracted magic number as `CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE`\n**Mass Change**: 116 → 111 (delta -5)\n**Tests**: All passing (13 passed, 30 todo)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-18-36_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 13\nRecent Green phase: Added cursed item surcharge (50% on item base premium). Restructured calculateBasePremium to handle non-component items with per-item modifiers, then component block pricing from counts.\n\nRun autonomously, return after completion.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 13\nRecent Green phase: Added cursed item surcharge (50% on item base premium). Restructured calculateBasePremium to handle non-component items with per-item modifiers, then component block pricing from counts.\n\nRun autonomously, return after completion."}],"timestamp":1784949749640},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the implementation and test files to understand the"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5d8b401b0e4d415787bfa1a0","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0e0110c5919947598f8a90db","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":222,"output":98,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6464,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949749660,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-48ea226c-eee1-4d0c-94b5-dac3a64274b9","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5d8b401b0e4d415787bfa1a0","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Quote and claim processing logic\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\n}\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nconst ITEM_PRICES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT = 3;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst calculateBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const counts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n  }\n\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(item.type)) {\n      // Handle components via counts (deferred)\n      continue;\n    }\n    let itemBase = ITEM_PRICES[item.type] || 0;\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemBase += itemBase * 0.5;\n    }\n    total += itemBase;\n  }\n\n  // Handle component block pricing\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(counts)) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(type)) {\n      if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT) {\n        total += BLOCK_PRICE;\n      } else {\n        total += count * (ITEM_PRICES[type] || 0);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): unknown => {\n  const results: unknown[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const basePremium = calculateBasePremium(step.items);\n      results.push({ premium: basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE });\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949750436},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0e0110c5919947598f8a90db","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office\", () => {\n  // === Quote: Item base premiums ===\n  it(\"should return 5 G for empty item list — only processing fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 105 G for a single sword — 100 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 105 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 65 G for a single amulet — 60 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 65 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 85 G for a single staff — 80 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 85 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 45 G for a single potion — 40 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 45 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 30 G for a single component (rune) — 25 G base + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 30 }] });\n  });\n\n  // === Quote: Component blocks ===\n  it(\"should return 55 G for 2 runes — 50 G base, no block applies\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 55 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 65 G for 3 runes — 60 G block base premium + 5 G fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 65 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 105 G for 4 runes — 100 G base, no block (requires exactly 3)\", () => {\