 - `+=` appears 4 times = 4\n  - Total invocations: **16** × 2 = **32**\n\n- **Conditionals**: `if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has...)` → `continue` (1), `if (item.cursed)` (2), `if (item.enchantment >=...)` (3), `if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has...)` (4), `if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT)` (5) = **5 conditionals** × 4 = **20**\n\n- **Loops**: `for (const item of items)` (1), `for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(counts))` (2) = **2 loops** × 5 = **10**\n\n- **Assignments**: `counts[item.type] = ...` (1), `let itemBase = ...` (2), `itemBase += ...` (3), `itemBase += ...` (4), `total += itemBase` (5), `total += BLOCK_PRICE` (6), `total += count * ...` (7) = **7 assignments** × 6 = **42**\n\n**Total Mass**: 4 + 7 + 32 + 20 + 10 + 42 = **115**\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules\n\n### Rule 1: Tests Pass ✅\nAll 15 tests pass. Good.\n\n### Rule 2: Reveals Intent\n\nIssues I see:\n1. **The two-pass approach is confusing**: First pass counts components and calculates non-component items; second pass handles component block pricing. This splits related logic across two loops. The intent — \"calculate item total with special component block pricing\" — is obscured.\n2. **`itemBase` is a `let` variable that gets mutated** via `+=` multiple times. While clear enough with `originalBase`, it's a mutation-heavy pattern.\n3. **The `continue` early in the component-pricing loop** skips surcharge calculation, which is correct but makes the flow harder to follow — you have to trace which branch a component goes through.\n4. **`const counts: Record<string, number> = {}`** is only used for component block pricing but is populated for all items.\n\nPotential improvement: Restructure to separate component items from non-component items, reducing the dual-pass complexity.\n\n### Rule 3: No Duplication\n\nLooking for duplication:\n1. **`ITEM_PRICES[item.type] || 0`** appears twice — in the first loop and in the component fallback of the second loop. This is a lookup pattern duplication.\n2. **`(counts[item.type] || 0) + 1`** is a count-increment pattern.\n3. The surcharge logic (`originalBase * rate`, `+=`) is structurally duplicated for cursed and enchantment.\n\n### Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n\nThe function has two separate loops that both care about `BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS`. This could potentially be one loop with cleaner grouping.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Implement Refactoring\n\nI'll focus on **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)** first: extract a helper to calculate a single item's price with surcharges, which will also reduce duplication (Rule 3). This makes the code more self-documenting.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f517ccb802f941308f2bb0ce","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const calculateBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const counts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts[item.type] = (counts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(item.type)) continue;\n    let itemBase = ITEM_PRICES[item.type] || 0;\n    const originalBase = itemBase;\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemBase += originalBase * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    if (item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n      itemBase += originalBase * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    total += itemBase;\n  }\n\n  // Handle component block pricing\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(counts)) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(type)) {\n      if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT) {\n        total += BLOCK_PRICE;\n      } else {\n        total += count * (ITEM_PRICES[type] || 0);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return total;\n};","newText":"const itemPrice = (itemType: string): number => ITEM_PRICES[itemType] || 0;\n\nconst applySurcharges = (basePrice: number, item: Item): number => {\n  let price = basePrice;\n  if (item.cursed) {\n    price += basePrice * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  }\n  if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    price += basePrice * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  }\n  return price;\n};\n\nconst calculateBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const nonComponentItems: Item[] = [];\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      nonComponentItems.push(item);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let total = 0;\n\n  for (const item of nonComponentItems) {\n    const base = itemPrice(item.type);\n    total += applySurcharges(base, item);\n  }\n\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(componentCounts)) {\n    if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT) {\n      total += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      total += count * itemPrice(type);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return total;\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":454,"output":2974,"cacheRead":9728,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13156,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949842368,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3c749372-b5de-4902-afad-e0361bcf53bd","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f517ccb802f941308f2bb0ce","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  46 const BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n  47 const EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT = 3;\n  48 const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n  49 \n+ 50 const itemPrice = (itemType: string): number => ITEM_PRICES[itemType] || 0;\n+ 51 \n+ 52 const applySurcharges = (basePrice: number, item: Item): number => {\n+ 53   let price = basePrice;\n+ 54   if (item.cursed) {\n+ 55     price += basePrice * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n+ 56   }\n+ 57   if (item.enchantment !== undefined && item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n+ 58     price +