deed on the item base premium sum.\n\nBut my current code: I add first insurance surcharge to `quotePremium` which is `calculateBasePremium()` which includes curse/enchantment surcharges. That's incorrect!\n\nLet me check: calculateBasePremium computes item base prices plus per-item modifiers (curse, enchantment). The first insurance should apply to the raw item base premiums (before per-item modifiers).\n\nSimilarly for loyalty. Let me recheck the integration example:\n\"100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment − 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance − 15 follow-up = 155\"\n\nThat breaks down: base=100, curse=50, enchant=30, loyalty=-20 (20% of 100), first=+10 (10% of 100), follow-up=-15 (15% of 100). All applied to base 100.\n\nSo all policy-wide modifiers (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up) apply to the sum of raw item base prices, NOT to the items-plus-item-modifiers total. Let me fix this.\n\nActually wait, for the current test it doesn't matter yet - the sword has no curse/enchantment, so calculateBasePremium returns 100 (just the raw base). The test should pass... Let me run:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f064c4d6d5b540e1916c4e00","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-18-36_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":179,"output":787,"cacheRead":56832,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":57798,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949957879,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-591c30f4-5dbe-440b-9ea0-a5dc7f91ce38","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f064c4d6d5b540e1916c4e00","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-18-36_claim-office-example-mappin