wcomer with cursed sword: 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first insurance = 160\"\n- Raw base = 100. First insurance = 10% of 100 = 10. So first_insurance is on raw base, not cursed-adjusted base.\n\nBut curse and enchantment are \"item-specific modifiers\" that modify the item's premium before being summed into the policy base. So:\n\nitem contribution = base_price + (cursed ? 50%) + (enchant≥5 ? 30%)\npolicy_base = sum of item contributions\nfinal = policy_base + first_insurance(10% of raw_sum) - loyalty(20% of raw_sum) + fee\n\nWait, that doesn't work either. Let me look at example 2:\n\"100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment − 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance − 15 follow-up = 155\"\n\nRaw base = 100. curse = 50 (50% of 100). enchant = 30 (30% of 100). loyalty = -20 (-20% of 100). first = +10 (10% of 100). follow-up = -15 (-15% of 100).\n\nSo ALL modifiers (including curse and enchantment) are computed off the raw base of 100. Curse is not 50% of 100+... it's literally 50% of 100 = 50. Enchantment is 30% of 100 = 30. Loyalty is 20% of 100 = 20. First insurance is 10% of 100 = 10. Follow-up is 15% of 100 = 15.\n\nThey're all computed independently on the same raw base 100. Then summed: 100 + 50 + 30 - 20 + 10 - 15 = 155. Plus fee 5 = 160.\n\nSo the surcharge computation for curse/enchantment/loyalty/first/follow-up is all done on RAW item base prices, not on each other. They don't compound.\n\nBut wait: my current implementation for curse and enchantment computes them as itemBase * rate which uses the correct raw base (since I fixed originalBase). Then first insurance computes quotePremium * rate which would compound.\n\nThe fix: I need to compute rawSum (just sum of raw item base prices + block-adjusted component sums), then compute all policy-wide modifiers (first_insurance, loyalty, follow-up) as a percentage of rawSum, then add item-specific surcharges on top.\n\nActually let me reconsider. Looking at the example once more:\n\n\"100 base + 50 curse + 30 high enchantment − 20 loyalty + 10 first insurance − 15 follow-up\"\n\nThe item-specific modifiers (curse, enchantment) and policy-wide modifiers (loyalty, first, follow-up) are all listed as separate line items added to the base. They're ALL computed independently on the raw base of 100.\n\nSo the cleanest implementation: compute raw symbol base (sum of ITEM_PRICES), then add each modifier as a percentage of that raw base.\n\nBut... the cursed + plain amulet example says: \"a policy covers a cursed sword (base premium 100 G) and a plain amulet (base premium 60 G) → policy base premium 160 G; the cursed surcharge adds 50 G (50 % of the cursed sword's base premium, not of the policy total) → 210 G\".\n\nSo cursed surcharge is 50% of the cursed item's base, not the policy total. And from the modifier scope rules: \"item-specific modifiers (cursed, high enchantment) apply to the base premium of the affected item; policy-wide modifiers (loyalty, first insurance, follow-up contract) apply to the policy base premium\"\n\nSo: \n- cursed surcharge = 0.5 × cursed_item_base (per item)\n- high enchantment surcharge = 0.3 × enchanted_item_base (per item)\n- loyalty discount = 0.2 × sum_of_all_item_bases\n- first insurance = 0.1 × sum_of_all_item_bases\n- follow-up = 0.15 × sum_of_all_item_bases\n\nAnd they're all additive/subtractive, not compounding.\n\nLet me now fix the implementation to separate item-specific modifiers from policy-wide modifiers, and compute all from raw item base sums. Then fix all the test expectations.\n\nThe tests currently expect values without first-insurance surcharge. Now that I've added it, I must update them. But I also need to fix the compounding issue (first insurance should be on raw base, not on cursed-adjusted base).\n\nLet me just fix all test expectations and the implementation at once. Let me compute the corrected expected values:\n\nAll tests with yearsWithMHPCO=0 (which is ALL tests except loyalty test):\n- first_insurance = 10% of raw_sum\n\nTest 1: empty list → raw_sum=0, first_insurance=0, fee=5 → 5 ✓ (unchanged)\nTest 2: sword → raw_sum=100, first=10, base=100, total=100+10+5=115 (was 105)\nTest 3: amulet → raw=60, first=6, base=60+6+5=71 (was 65)\nTest 4: staff → raw=80, first=8, base=80+8+5=93 (was 85)\nTest 5: potion → raw=40, first=4, base=40+4+5=49 (was 45)\nTest 6: rune → raw=25, first=2.5, base=25+2.5+5=32.5 (was 30) — this will need rounding!\nTest 7: 2 runes → raw=50, first=5, base=50+5+5=60 (was 55)\nTest 8: 3 runes (block) → raw=60, first=6, base=60+6+5=71 (was 65)\nTest 9: 4 runes → raw=100, first=10, base=100+10+5=115 (was 105)\nTest 10: 7 runes → raw=175, first=17.5, base=175+17.5+5=197.5 (was 180) — rounding: up = 198\nTest 11: 2 runes + 1 moonstone → raw=75, first=7.5, base=75+7.5+5=87.5 (was 80) — rounding: up = 88\nTest 12: 3 runes + 3 moonstones → raw=120, first=12, base=120+12+5=137 (was 125)\nTest 13: cursed sword → raw=100, curse=50, first=10, base=100+50+10=160+5=165 (was 155)\nTest 14: enchant 5 sword → raw=100, enchant=30, first=10, base=100+30+10=140+5=145 (was 135)\nTest 15: cursed enchant 5 → raw=100, curse=50, enchant=30, first=10, base=100+50+30+10=190+5=195 (was 185)\nTest 16: enchant 4 → raw=100, first=10, base=100+10=110+5=115 (was 105)\nTest 17: loyalty 2yrs → raw=100, first=10, loyalty=-20, base=100+10-20=90+5=95 (was 85)\n\nWait, the test 17 (loyalty) uses yearsWithMHPCO=2, so loyalty applies AND first insurance applies. The expected should be 100 + 10 (first) - 20 (loyalty) = 90 + 5 = 95.\n\nBut the current test says 85. That's wrong now because first insurance also applies. Let me fix all of these.\n\nHowever, there's also the rounding issue: \"All amounts are rounded to whole G in the MHPCO's favor.\" Premiums round UP. So 32.5 → 33, 87.5 → 88, 197.5 → 198.\n\nNow, my current implementation doesn't do rounding yet. The rounding test is test 23. But test 6 (rune, 25 base) now involves first insurance which gives 2.5, so 25+2.5+5=32.5 which should round UP to 33. The current implementation would compute 32.5, but the test expects 30. Hmm.\n\nFor now, let me fix the implementation to NOT compound first insurance with item surcharges, then update test expectations. I'll also need to handle the rounding issue for the non-integer results.\n\nLet me first fix the implementation to properly separate raw_sum vs item-adjusted total, and apply policy-wide modifiers to raw_sum only.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2b3210dbf19349608c4dc8cf","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-18-36_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":9026,"output":2155,"cacheRead":57600,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":68781,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949969320,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-4402a216-e17b-4f4e-901f-904b373767f2","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2b3210dbf19349608c4dc8cf","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Quote and claim processing logic\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\n}\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nconst ITEM_PRICES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nconst EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT = 3;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst calculateBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const nonComponentItems: Item[] = [];\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      nonComponentItems.push(item);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let total = 0;\n\n  for (const item of nonComponentItems) {\n    const basePrice = ITEM_PRICES[item.type] || 0;\n    let itemTotal = basePrice;\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemTotal += basePrice * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    if (item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n      itemTotal += basePrice * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    total += itemTotal;\n  }\n\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(componentCounts)) {\n    if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT) {\n      total += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      total += count * (ITEM_PRICES[type] || 0);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return total;\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): unknown => {\n  const results: unknown[] = [];\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      let quotePremium = calculateBasePremium(step.items);\n      quotePremium += quotePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n      if (scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD) {\n        quotePremium -= quotePremium * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n      }\n      results.push({ premium: quotePremium + PROCESSING_FEE });\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784949986451},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to restructure. The `calculateBasePremium` currently includes item-specific surcharges (curse, enchantment) in its result. But policy-wide modifiers should apply to the raw item base sum.\n\nLet me redesign: `calculateBasePremium` returns { baseSum, itemSurcharges }, then processScenario applies policy-wide modifiers to baseSum and adds item surcharges.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6f3a9d11bddc4d0a8cfb3c10","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"const calculateQuote = (items: Item[]): { baseSum: number; itemSurcharges: number } => {\n  const nonComponentItems: Item[] = [];\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      nonComponentItems.push(item);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let baseSum = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of nonComponentItems) {\n    const basePrice = ITEM_PRICES[item.type] || 0;\n    baseSum += basePrice;\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemSurcharges += basePrice * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    if (item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n      itemSurcharges += basePrice * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(componentCounts)) {\n    const price = ITEM_PRICES[type] || 0;\n    if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT) {\n      baseSum += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      baseSum += count * price;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { baseSum, itemSurcharges };\n};","oldText":"const calculateBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const nonComponentItems: Item[] = [];\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      nonComponentItems.push(item);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let total = 0;\n\n  for (const item of nonComponentItems) {\n    const basePrice = ITEM_PRICES[item.type] || 0;\n    let itemTotal = basePrice;\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemTotal += basePrice * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    if (item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n      itemTotal += basePrice * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    total += itemTotal;\n  }\n\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(componentCounts)) {\n    if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT) {\n      total += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      total += count * (ITEM_PRICES[type] || 0);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return total;\n};"}],"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-18-36_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":6058,"output":901,"cacheRead":63488,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":70447,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784949986456,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-159e955d-aa98-43ba-ba4d-eabde80d6bfe","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6f3a9d11bddc4d0a8cfb3c10","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-18-36_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  51 \n  52 const EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT = 3;\n  53 const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n  54 \n- 55 const calculateBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n+ 55 const calculateQuote = (items: Item[]): { baseSum: number; itemSurcharges: number } => {\n  56   const nonComponentItems: Item[] = [];\n  57   const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n  58 \n  59   for (const item of items) {\n     ...\n  63       nonComponentItems.push(item);\n  64     }\n  65   }\n  66 \n- 67   let total = 0;\n+ 67   let baseSum = 0;\n+ 68   let itemSurcharges = 0