unted differently) = let me be precise:\n\nOriginal module-level bindings included 13 bindings: the 12 consts plus the 1 extra was... I had 13 earlier. Let me recount. The original had: ITEM_PRICES, CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE, HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD, BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS, BLOCK_PRICE, FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE, LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE, LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD, FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE, EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT, PROCESSING_FEE = 12. Then `calculateQuote` binding + `processScenario` binding = 2 more, so 14 module-level bindings. But that's double-counting if I also count them inside functions. Let me just keep the same treatment.\n\nActually, the cleanest way: module-level constants are counted once. Function-level bindings are counted in their function. The mass is primarily about the function's internal complexity.\n\n**calculateQuote: 89 → 81 (delta: -8)**\n**Overall: roughly 151 → 143**\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Merged two loops in `calculateQuote` — eliminated the `nonCategoryItems` intermediate array\n\n**What changed**:\n- Instead of separating items into `nonComponentItems` and `componentCounts` in three loops (filter → price non-components → price components), now we do it in two loops (classify-and-price → price components)\n- Removed `nonComponentItems: Item[]` binding\n- Removed one loop (5 mass)\n- Removed one invocation (`push`) (2 mass)\n- The `ITEM_PRICES[item.type]` lookup now happens in only one place rather than being duplicated\n\n**Simple Design Rules checked**:\n- **Rule 1**: ✅ All 19 tests pass\n- **Rule 2**: ✅ Intent still clear — the code reveals that non-component items get priced immediately when encountered\n- **Rule 3**: ✅ Removed duplication of `ITEM_PRICES[item.type]` lookup; removed the unnecessary intermediate collection\n- **Rule 4**: ✅ Fewer elements (2 loops instead of 3, one less binding, one less push invocation)\n\n**Mass change**: calculateQuote 89 → 81 (-8). Total estimated: 151 → 143 (-8).\n\n---\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Merged `calculateQuote`'s first and second loops (classification + non-component pricing) into a single pass, eliminating the `nonComponentItems` intermediate array and its iteration.\n**Mass Change**: 151 → 143 (delta: -8)\n**Tests**: All 19 passing, 24 todo remaining."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_03-18-36_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_deepseek-v4-pro-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added follow-up contract discount (15% for second+ quotes). Tracked quoteCount to determine if it's a follow-up contract.\n\nRun autonomously, return after completion.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 19\nRecent Green phase: Added follow-up contract discount (15% for second+ quotes). Tracked quoteCount to determine if it's a follow-up contract.\n\nRun autonomously, return after completion."}],"timestamp":1784950046927},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nI'll start by reading the implementation and test files to understand the current state of"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8283da3c5980470cace73633","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6e4a4231b6d4480eb1b0fc4a","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"tensorx/deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":214,"output":101,"cacheRead":6144,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6459,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784950046947,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5cef5085-4662-4e87-a151-771729d723f7","responseModel":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8283da3c5980470cace73633","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"// Quote and claim processing logic\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: { cause: string; damages: Damage[] };\n}\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nconst ITEM_PRICES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\n\nconst BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD = 2;\n\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT = 3;\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\n\nconst calculateQuote = (items: Item[]): { baseSum: number; itemSurcharges: number } => {\n  const nonComponentItems: Item[] = [];\n  const componentCounts: Record<string, number> = {};\n\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (BLOCK_PRICE_COMPONENTS.has(item.type)) {\n      componentCounts[item.type] = (componentCounts[item.type] || 0) + 1;\n    } else {\n      nonComponentItems.push(item);\n    }\n  }\n\n  let baseSum = 0;\n  let itemSurcharges = 0;\n\n  for (const item of nonComponentItems) {\n    const basePrice = ITEM_PRICES[item.type] || 0;\n    baseSum += basePrice;\n    if (item.cursed) {\n      itemSurcharges += basePrice * CURSED_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n    if (item.enchantment >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n      itemSurcharges += basePrice * HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n    }\n  }\n\n  for (const [type, count] of Object.entries(componentCounts)) {\n    const price = ITEM_PRICES[type] || 0;\n    if (count === EXACT_BLOCK_COUNT) {\n      baseSum += BLOCK_PRICE;\n    } else {\n      baseSum += count * price;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { baseSum, itemSurcharges };\n};\n\nexport const processScenario = (scenario: Scenario): unknown => {\n  const results: unknown[] = [];\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  for (const step of scenario.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const { baseSum, itemSurcharges } = calculateQuote(step.items);\n      let quotePremium = baseSum + itemSurcharges;\n      quotePremium += baseSum * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n      if (scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_YEARS_THRESHOLD) {\n        quotePremium -= baseSum * LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n      }\n      quoteCount++;\n      if (quoteCount > 1) {\n        quotePremium -= baseSum * FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n      }\n      const premium = Math.ceil(quotePremium + PROCESSING_FEE);\n      results.push({ premium });\n    }\n  }\n  return { results };\n};"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784950047783},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_6e4a4231b6d4480eb1b0fc4a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office\", () => {\n  // === Quote: Item base premiums ===\n  it(\"should return 5 G for empty item list — only processing fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 115 G for a single sword — 100 base + 10 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 71 G for a single amulet — 60 base + 6 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 93 G for a single staff — 80 base + 8 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 93 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 49 G for a single potion — 40 base + 4 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 49 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 33 G for a single rune — 25 base + 2.5 first insurance + 5 fee, rounded up\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 33 }] });\n  });\n\n  // === Quote: Component blocks ===\n  it(\"should return 60 G for 2 runes — 50 base + 5 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 60 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 71 G for 3 runes — 60 block + 6 first insurance + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 71 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 115 G for 4 runes — 100 base + 10 first + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }\n        ] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 198 G for 7 runes — 175 base + 17.5 first + 5 fee, rounded up\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: Array(7).fill({ type: \"rune\" }) }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 198 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 88 G for 2 runes + 1 moonstone — 75 base + 7.5 first + 5 fee, rounded up\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }\n        ] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 88 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should return 137 G for 3 runes + 3 moonstones — 120 base + 12 first + 5 fee\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }\n        ] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 137 }] });\n  });\n\n  // === Quote: Premium modifiers ===\n  it(\"should apply 50% cursed surcharge — cursed sword: 100 base + 50 curse + 10 first + 5 fee = 165 G\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 165 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should apply 30% high-enchantment surcharge — enchant 5 sword: 100 base + 30 enchant + 10 first + 5 fee = 145 G\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 5 }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 145 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should apply both cursed and high-enchantment surcharges: 100 + 50 + 30 + 10 first + 5 fee = 195 G\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true, enchantment: 5 }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 195 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should NOT apply high-enchantment surcharge to sword with enchantment 4: 100 + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\", enchantment: 4 }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should apply 20% loyalty discount for customer with exactly 2 years: 100 + 10 first - 20 loyalty + 5 fee = 95 G\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 95 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should apply 10% first-insurance surcharge: 100 + 10 first + 5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"should apply 15% follow-up contract discount on second quote\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(scenario);\n    // First quote: 100 + 10 (first) + 5 = 115. Second quote: 100 + 10 (first) - 15 (follow-up) + 5 = 100\n    expect(result).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 115 }, { premium: 100 }] });\n  });\n\n  // === Quote: Multi-item modifier scope ===\n  it.todo(\"should apply cursed surcharge only to the cursed item, not the full policy\");\n\n  // === Quote: Integration examples ===\n  it.todo(\"should return 165 G for newcomer (0 years, no previous) with cursed sword\");\n\n  it.todo(\"should return 160 G for long-standing customer (3 years, second contract) with cursed sword enchant 7\");\n\n  // === Quote: Rounding ===\n  it.todo(\"should round premium up in MHPCO's favor — 197.5 G becomes 19